      children: "Pipeline patterns work exceptionally well for ETL-style workflows, content processing, and compliance workflows where each stage represents a distinct regulatory or business requirement. They become cumbersome when workflows need significant backtracking, when stage order varies by input type, or when parallel execution of independent stages is critical for performance."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h3, {
